{"title":"Lab Technologist Roadmap","role":"Lab Technologist","summary":"A Medical Laboratory Technologist performs laboratory testing on biological specimens such as blood, urine, body fluids, tissues, and other clinical samples. The role supports physicians by generating accurate laboratory information used for diagnosis, treatment decisions, disease monitoring, and screening.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Medical Laboratory Technology (BMLT / B.Sc MLT)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Medical Laboratory Technologist performs laboratory testing on biological specimens such as blood, urine, body fluids, tissues, and other clinical samples. The role supports physicians by generating accurate laboratory information used for diagnosis, treatment decisions, disease monitoring, and screening."},{"type":"p","text":"A BMLT/B.Sc MLT graduate can develop expertise across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical biochemistry"},{"text":"Hematology"},{"text":"Clinical pathology"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Immunology"},{"text":"Serology"},{"text":"Histopathology"},{"text":"Blood banking"},{"text":"Molecular diagnostics"},{"text":"Laboratory quality management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest employability combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Laboratory Science","Diagnostic Testing","Quality Control","Biosafety","Instrumentation","Digital Laboratory Systems"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Basic laboratory science"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Technical Development"},{"text":"Clinical laboratory disciplines"}],[{"text":"2030–2032"},{"text":"Internship"},{"text":"Hospital/diagnostic laboratory exposure"}],[{"text":"2032–2035"},{"text":"En